<title>BELGIUM: Only Greece to miss EU deficit/GDP ratio in 98-EU.</title>
<headline>Only Greece to miss EU deficit/GDP ratio in 98-EU.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission, looking beyond the 1997 year in which it must decide which countries qualify for the single currency, predicted that all but Greece would meet the three percent budget deficit to GDP criteria in 1998.</p>
<p>In its economic forecasts report, the Commission saw the follow debt to GDP ratio in 1998.</p>
<p>Belgium - 2.5 pct</p>
<p>Denmark - 0.3</p>
<p>Germany - 2.4</p>
<p>Greece - 5.3</p>
<p>Spain - 2.8</p>
<p>France - 2.9</p>
<p>Ireland - 0.5</p>
<p>Italy - 3.0</p>
<p>Luxembourg - 0.9</p>
<p>Netherlands - 2.0</p>
<p>Austria - 2.9</p>
<p>Portugal - 2.9</p>
<p>Finland - 1.4</p>
<p>Sweden  - 1.0</p>
<p>Britain - 2.2 -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
